.TH "NOIRPASS.TOML" "5" "2026-11-25" "noirpass 1.0.2" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
noirpass.toml \- Noirpass configuration file (config.toml)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/noirpass/config.toml\fR
.PP
\fI~/.local/share/noirpass/config.toml\fR
.PP
\fI<STORE_DIR>/config.toml\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Noirpass stores configuration in \fBconfig.toml\fR inside its store directory.
By default this is \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/noirpass/config.toml\fR when
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR is set to an absolute path, or
\fI~/.local/share/noirpass/config.toml\fR otherwise. Passing
\fB\-\-store\-dir\fR or setting \fBNOIRPASS_STORE\fR selects
\fI<STORE_DIR>/config.toml\fR instead.
.PP
\fBnoirpass init \-\-recipient <FILE|\->\fR creates \fBconfig.toml\fR with
mode \fB0600\fR inside a \fB0700\fR store directory. Recipient fields are
managed by Noirpass; edit only documented runtime settings.
.SH SETTINGS
\fBidle_exit\fR (integer, default \fB300\fR, minimum \fB\-1\fR)
.RS
Controls how the daemon exits when no transport session is open and the
temporary \fBsession\fR collection is empty:
.TP
\fB\-1\fR
Keep the daemon running until a signal (\fBSIGINT\fR/\fBSIGTERM\fR), session
bus disconnect, or fatal store error.
.TP
\fB0\fR
Exit after the first completed Noirpass application method or property
handler, once no handler is active, no transport session is open, and no
temporary secret remains.
.TP
\fIPositive integer\fR
Exit after this many seconds without Noirpass application activity, once no
handler is active, no transport session is open, and no temporary secret
remains.
.PP
Default is \fB300\fR. An existing \fBconfig.toml\fR without \fBidle_exit\fR
uses the same default. Re\-running \fBnoirpass init\fR for the same primary
recipient preserves the current deserialized value. Command\-line
\fB\-\-idle\-exit <VALUE>\fR overrides configuration for one daemon
invocation.
.PP
A temporary secret in the \fBsession\fR collection deliberately pins the
daemon so Secret Service clients requesting \(lqremember for this session\(rq
keep that secret until they delete it or the daemon/login session ends. Calls
managed directly by \fBzbus\fR, including \fBorg.freedesktop.DBus.Peer.Ping\fR
and \fBorg.freedesktop.DBus.Introspectable.Introspect\fR, do not count as
Noirpass application activity.
.RE
.SH MANAGED FIELDS
These fields are written by \fBnoirpass init\fR and validated on startup and
maintenance:
.TP
\fBversion\fR (integer, currently \fB1\fR)
Persisted configuration format version.
.TP
\fBrecipient_fingerprint\fR (string)
Expected uppercase hex primary OpenPGP fingerprint of the store recipient.
.TP
\fBrecipient_cert\fR (string, default \fBkeys/recipient.pgp\fR)
Store\-relative path to the stored binary recipient certificate; must contain
only normal relative path components inside the store directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
Exit after the first Noirpass handler finishes with no transport session or
temporary secret:
.RS
.nf
idle_exit = 0
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keep the daemon running:
.RS
.nf
idle_exit = \-1
.fi
.RE
.PP
Exit after ten inactive minutes:
.RS
.nf
idle_exit = 600
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBnoirpass\fR(1)
